						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">Our alliance pretty much uses what justyce wrote~ In fact her post looks like a post i wrote to defend our policy when someone wanted to debate it.&nbsp; I even used the line about how we all got here only with the guilds effort so deciding now that your an independent agent is wrong.&nbsp; I took a more critical tone though when i said its impractical to have a mob sometimes be DKP and sometimes not be DKP.&nbsp; Either we always hit them pointed or we never hit them as an official target at all. Its impractical to sometimes not do a mob on points, but not on tuesdays when an officers there... That will breed rampant jealousy in about 2.5 seconds. In the end I was most concerned about what puts the most qvic loot in our guildees hands after you conclude that it has to be one or the other (pointed or not pointed) to be practical.&nbsp; I used that with a be careful what you wish for tone. <br /><br />In general if any guild moves from a dkp msha to a nondkp msha i think it will hinge upon whether or not they desire mshas to be a raid target ever again.&nbsp; Once it ceases to be a viable raid target then it becomes more practical to say FFA it.<br /><br />Im not an officer and may not speak for them but ive done some thinking about the msha issue it seems to come up for every guild eventually.</td>
