						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">toasties:<br /><a href="http://quellious-collective.com/permafrost/forums/viewtopic.php?t=5897" target="_blank">http://quellious-collective.com/permafrost/forums/viewtopic.php?t=5897</a><br /><br />Flaming died down this last year and a half alot.   Though for toasties reference that flame i linked the big one... none of the players are in the same position anymore.  An LC person started it.  LC were ahead of the server in the elemental planes.  <br /><br />One day before the 72 person change vis,Wraith/rev zergged the living fugg out of the warlord to get elemental.  In fact us three guilds were the reason in large part that encounter got changed.<br /><br />So an LC member flamed Vis/Wraith/Rev and it was on from there.<br /><br />But!  LC is no more.  Just a few months ago LC disbanded and has been sucked up into.. wraith rev and vis!  <br /><br />Now where did explicit go you might ask? Cause explicit was in the flaming fray too. Explicit was originally basically a vis spinter guild with a really hardcore bent.  They sucked up other peeps though cause of that.  Explicit eventually got ahead of LC but at the time of this thread they were behind everyone.  Eventually though much later they joined vis maior and took over leadership of vis.<br /><br />So there you have it.<br /><br />Though our most imfamous flame bait was a guild leader deleveling a main tank that left and denying it for a year only to admit it after about a year of constant flaming and getting banned~  It was particularly devisive because guild leaders are good at rallying people around them in their support! And lots of people came to bat and said &quot;if he says he didnt delevel him he didnt delevel him&quot; That was good times!</td>
