		<table border="0" width="85%" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="0" class="bordercolor" align="center">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%">
					<table border="0" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" class="bordercolor" align="center">
						<tr class="titlebg">
							<td align="left" style="padding: 0 1ex;">
								13
							</td>
							<td width="75%" align="left">
								&nbsp;<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php#1">General Category</a> / <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?board=1.0">General Discussion</a> / <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1507.15#msg15995">Re: Question about Plane of Time</a>
							</td>
							<td align="right" style="padding: 0 1ex; white-space: nowrap;">
								on: March 30, 2005, 02:45:32 pm
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">The only major issue with a rotated time will be all the guilds that want to reserve the right to do it but dont want to do it every time their rotation comes up.<br /><br />could be harder then back in the day.  Im sure no guild will say with a straight face that they wont do time ever.  So youll almost certainly have to rotate those guilds expect a large number of days they pass on.  And of course the big wild card is if one of the guilds that doesnt do time much doesnt care about the rotation.  Though I wouldnt want to be the first guild on the server to screw the first attempt at a rotation.<br /><br />Trust me though... theres probably someone out there giggling at the idea~<br /><br />Whatever scheme you start thinking about be mindful of how its going to treat the people that dont farm time but do time occasionally as that will be a big factor in whether it works.<br />[im not a guild leader]<br /></td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td colspan="3" class="windowbg2" align="right">
							</td>
						</tr>
					</table>
