					<table border="0" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" class="bordercolor" align="center">
						<tr class="titlebg">
							<td align="left" style="padding: 0 1ex;">
								14
							</td>
							<td width="75%" align="left">
								&nbsp;<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php#1">General Category</a> / <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?board=1.0">General Discussion</a> / <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1507.15#msg15989">Re: Question about Plane of Time</a>
							</td>
							<td align="right" style="padding: 0 1ex; white-space: nowrap;">
								on: March 30, 2005, 02:25:01 pm
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">We had a rotation on Quellious when it was 5 guilds actively farming. (LC, VM, Exp, CF, Wraith/rev) [Exp merged with VM since and LC disbanded]. Except Cold Fury didnt participate in the rotation because they were aussie time they took the 2nd instance for themselves at 2am.&nbsp; <br /><br /><br />Not rotating time is insane imo.&nbsp; You can sanely FFA everything in the game except for a contested time.&nbsp; FFA&#039;n a contested time is recipe for pure hate.<br /><br />The other historical rotations on quellious were rotated attempts at elemental gods.&nbsp; And rotated Qvic.&nbsp; Rotated qvic fell apart when Lotus Cult disbanded.&nbsp; There was no need/interest.<br /><br />Quellious basically has a long history of rotating stuff but currently theres no real need as nobody is bumping heads at any content level.&nbsp; <br /><br /><br /><br /></td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td colspan="3" class="windowbg2" align="right">
							</td>
						</tr>
